>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.Y.M SHAFA</td>\n                <td>₦1,780.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TMDK</td>\n                <td>₦1,675.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>OBAT OIL</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PRUDENT OGHARA</td>\n                <td>₦1,740.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>BULK STRATEGIC</td>\n                <td>₦1,745.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Kenya, Ethiopia and Rwanda Eye 30% Stake in Dangote’s $17bn East Africa Refinery\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Kenya, Ethiopia and Rwanda have expressed interest in taking equity positions in Dangote Industries’ proposed refinery project in Kenya. Nigerian industrialist offering East African countries a combined 30% stake in the planned $17 billion facility. Kenya is considering a 10% interest valued at approximately $500 million.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/kenya-ethiopia-and-rwanda-eye-30-stake-in-dangotes-17bn-east-africa-refinery\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Climb for Second Week as Iran Crisis Raises Supply Risks\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude stood at $93.39 per barrel, down 0.42 per cent, while West Texas Intermediate (WTI) traded at $86.32 per barrel. The modest daily declines have not erased the broader weekly gains, with geopolitical risks continuing to provide support for prices.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-climb-for-second-week-as-iran-crisis-raises-supply-risks\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Crisis Drives Global EV Sales Higher as Oil Shock Persists\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Electric vehicles could account for about 25 per cent of the global vehicle fleet by 2040. Wood Mackenzie said faster EV adoption could have significant implications for the global oil industry. The resulting decline in road-transport fuel demand could force about 40 refineries worldwide to close earlier than previously expected.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-crisis-drives-global-ev-sales-higher-as-oil-shock-persists-2\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    BREAKING: Dangote Refinery Raises Petrol Gantry Price to ₦1,185/Litre\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Dangote Petroleum Refinery has raised its Premium Motor Spirit (PMS) gantry price by ₦20 per litre. The new price is effective midnight, August 21, 2026. The adjustment comes against a Lagos depot market where PMS is currently trading at ⁦1,200 perlitre.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/breaking-dangote-refinery-raises-petrol-gantry-price-to-1185litre\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Rise Nearly 3% as Trump Threatens Iran Backers\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    As of 11:30 a.m. WAT, Brent crude was trading at $93.82 per barrel, up $2.20 or 2.40% , while West Texas Intermediate (WTI) stood at $86.65 per barrel. The latest advance came after U.S. President Donald Trump announced what he described as the “most crushing economic operation” against Iran.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-rise-nearly-3-as-trump-threatens-iran-backers\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
